available lengths: 152cm, 155cm, 157cm, 159cm, 162cm, 155cm Wide, 157cm Wide, 159cm Wide, 162cm Wide
board type: All Mountain
flex: 3.5/10
flex type: Twin Flex (flexes the same in nose and tail for equal performance regular and switch)
rider level: Intermediate
shape: Twin (constructed exactly the same tip to tail for consistent performance in switch and regular)
camber type: PurePop (evolution of traditional camber with subtle flat zones outside feet to amplify pop and add playfulness, early rise tip and tail reduce catch and enhance float)
mounting system: The Channel (compatible with most major binding brands, works best with Burton EST bindings)
core: Super Fly II 700G (stronger and lighter woods targeted in specific areas for more pop and strength while reducing weight)
core zones: Dualzone EGD (wood grain along heel and toe edge in two unbroken zones perpendicular to rest of core for consistent edge hold and strength)
core sections: Squeezebox (thicker more powerful sections combined with thinner more flexible sections profiled throughout core for enhanced energy transfer, snappier and more stable)
laminate: Triax Glass (triaxial fibreglass for versatile flex and consistent response across all types of snowboarding)
base: Sintered (durable and highly porous base material for added strength and wax absorption for long lasting glide)
edges: Frostbite Edges (edges extend slightly under bindings for enhanced edge hold on hardpack and ice)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin reducing carbon footprint by 50% over conventional petroleum-based epoxies)
additional feature - Infinite Ride: Board is overbuilt in factory then broken down by machinery so it rides the same from day one to day 100
additional feature - Pro Tip: Tip and tail taper out at points reducing swing weight and promoting mobility
additional feature - Scoop: Exaggerated tip and tail scooping turns up edges for looser, more forgiving feel, catch-free fun on features and powder
pro rider association: Mark McMorris
also available in: Flying V bend (floatier, more forgiving feel)
average review rating: 5.0 out of 5
number of reviews: 3
review summary: Fun for groomers and park, nice pop off jumps, forgiving and not easy to catch edge, great for progressing beginners and intermediates, can get unstable at very high speed
